      "src": "/books/Guide/ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING/images/image_ylieop8.png"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "czuzuor",
      "content": "The book is structured into ten chapters covering the complete technical syllabus: DC Circuits, AC Circuits, Network Analysis, Electrical Machines, Transformers, Power Systems, Control Systems, Measurements, Power Electronics, and Analog &amp; Digital Electronics. Each chapter contains comprehensive theory with derivations, circuit diagrams, formula tables, worked examples, and practice MCQs."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y7hgij5",
      "content": "Every concept is explained from first principles so that the student can answer both straightforward formula-based questions and complex application-based questions. Special attention has been given to topics with the highest frequency in PSU exams — Transformers, Induction Motors, Power Factor, Network Theorems, Measuring Instruments, and Power Electronics."
    },
