    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "3uwpxww",
      "content": "<strong>Effect of Temperature on Resistance</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "50b9g76",
      "content": "Resistance of a conductor changes with temperature. For most metals (positive temperature coefficient), resistance increases with temperature."
    },
    {
      "id": "3smgxmj",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>R_T = R₀ (1 + α·T)        where α = temperature coefficient of resistance, T = temperature rise (°C)</strong></p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "jznqaf3",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Material</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Temperature Coefficient α (per °C)</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Nature</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Copper</p>",
            "<p>0.00393</p>",
            "<p>Positive — resistance increases with temp</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Aluminium</p>",
            "<p>0.00403</p>",
            "<p>Positive</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Silver</p>",
            "<p>0.0038</p>",
            "<p>Positive</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Carbon / Graphite</p>",
            "<p>−0.0005</p>",
            "<p>Negative — resistance decreases with temp</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
